  "instructions": {
    "en": "Imagine ordinary low-stakes work where both arrangements are permitted, can meet the stated task needs and provide equal safety, access and necessary information. Choose the arrangement you would currently prefer, not what you think an employer wants or what would make you better at the task. First and second switch positions across items. A midpoint means no clear preference; if the situation is irrelevant, cannot be judged or you prefer not to answer, choose unscored instead. Preferences can depend on the task. No company data are requested, and no organisational fit, competence or hiring score is calculated.",
    "zh": "想象普通、低影响的工作，两种安排都获准、能满足明示任务需要，并同样满足安全、无障碍与必要信息条件。选目前更愿意采用的安排，不猜雇主想要什么，也不选看起来更能证明能力的答案。第一、第二的顺序会换位。中点表示没有明确偏好；情境不相关、无法判断或不愿答时选不计分。偏好可能随任务变化。不收公司资料，不计算组织契合、胜任或招聘分数。"
  },
